
==============================================================================
  DIVERGENCE -- a conformance harness for payment integrations
==============================================================================
  Target : razorpay/razorpay-woocommerce v4.8.7, unmodified, 100,000+ installs
  Method : run the real plugin; check it against its vendor's own documentation

  Razorpay's documentation says this, verbatim:

      "Ideally, you should receive a webhook in the order in which the webhook events occur. However, you may not always receive the webhooks in the order."

  That sentence is a specification. Here it is as a test.

==============================================================================
  SAME TWO EVENTS. SAME SIGNATURES. ONLY THE ORDER DIFFERS.
==============================================================================

  authorization settles first
    payment.authorized  ->  refund.created
    order #476 ends:  WC-REFUNDED

  refund arrives first
    refund.created  ->  payment.authorized
    order #478 ends:  WC-PROCESSING

==============================================================================
  The same two events, delivered in the two orders the vendor says are both legal,
  leave the shop in two different states.

    wc-refunded    the customer got their money back
    wc-processing  PAID. Fulfil this order.

  In the second one the refund was silently discarded, and the shop is about to
  ship goods for an order that has already been refunded.
==============================================================================

==============================================================================
  WHY THIS IS NOT A RACE YOU COULD GET LUCKY WITH
==============================================================================
  payment.authorized is parked for a cron that only picks up rows older than 300s.
  Refunds are handled the moment they arrive.

      woo-razorpay.php:3393   rzp_webhook_notified_at < time()-300

  So any refund inside that five-minute window takes the losing path. Every time.

==============================================================================
  AND IT IS NOT A SCRIPT THAT PRINTS MY OWN BUGS
==============================================================================
  The same harness, the same property, against Razorpay's OTHER plugin:

      razorpay-woocommerce   Rs 499 order, Rs 1 paid  ->  RED    completes the order
      razorpay-edd           Rs 499 order, Rs 1 paid  ->  GREEN  refuses it

  A harness that says RED everywhere is a bug list. The GREEN is the point.
  (Run harness/matrix.py to see both live -- about 50 seconds.)

==============================================================================
  WHAT I GOT WRONG
==============================================================================
  INCIDENTS.md -- 17 dated entries, every time this project produced a wrong result.

    - a headline percentage that was an artefact of how I sampled
    - a citation I wrote myself and presented as a quotation from Razorpay
    - the harness reporting GREEN having measured nothing, four separate times
    - a false PASS from a plugin that was not running at all
    - 13 of 19 attacks I wrote against my OWN harness succeeded, the day before
      submission. All 19 pass now. tests/adversarial.py, ~2 seconds.

  Those are why every property now refuses to answer without evidence, and why
  check.py will not report a verdict unless its control arm moves a real order.
==============================================================================
  Everything here is reproducible: cd rig && ./setup.sh, then harness/check.py
==============================================================================
